With 200k synthetic target samples, `beta1=0.25` is a real improvement on this seed set, while lowering the sample fraction is not reliable. I’ll collect the final line and then test the best `beta1` region more narrowly.
codex
A likely next gain is at the last layer: instead of averaging `ReLU(z)` directly, compute the sample mean/variance of the final preactivation `z` and apply the Gaussian ReLU moment formula, or blend it with the direct sample mean. This keeps the same sampled hidden cloud but reduces last-layer Monte Carlo noise.
